Usage:
  nucleus migrate [flags] [<action> [args]]

Apply and manage SQL migrations against the configured database. Without an action, up runs.

Actions:
  up [n]         Apply every pending migration, or only the next n
  down [n]       Roll back the last migration, or the last n (destructive: --force or --yes in production)
  steps <n>      Apply n migrations forward, or roll back |n| when n is negative
  status         List every migration file with its applied/pending state
  drift          Report applied migrations whose .up.sql file is missing on disk; exits non-zero on drift
  reset          Roll back every applied migration (destructive)
  refresh        Roll back every applied migration, then apply all of them again (destructive)
  create <name>  Write an empty <timestamp>_<name>.up.sql/.down.sql pair; needs no database

Flags:
  -config string
    	Path to nucleus config file
  -database string
    	Database alias to use (defaults to database_default)
  -force
    	Force destructive actions (recommended in CI)
  -migrations string
    	Migrations directory (default "migrations")
  -yes
    	Auto-confirm destructive actions without prompt

Examples:
  nucleus migrate --config nucleus.yml
  nucleus migrate --config nucleus.yml status
  nucleus migrate --config nucleus.yml down 1
  nucleus migrate create add_users_table
